    {
      "id": "general-pairing-en-001",
      "text": "Wine and cheese pairing is a classic combination. Red wines (Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot) pair well with hard cheeses (Parmesan, Cheddar). White wines (Chardonnay, Riesling) pair with soft cheeses (Brie, Camembert). Sparkling wines go with any cheese. The key is to match the intensity of the wine with the intensity of the cheese.",
